# 17. WATERFALL STATE MACHINE

Implement an explicit state machine rather than using uncontrolled signal conditions.

Suggested states:

1. IDLE — No relevant directional sequence.
2. IMPULSE_DETECTED — Initial meaningful impulse observed.
3. MOMENTUM_CONFIRMED — Continuation conditions met.
4. PULLBACK_WATCH — Waiting for suitable retracement.
5. ENTRY_CANDIDATE — Setup conditions developing.
6. ENTRY_CONFIRMED — Required confirmation complete.
7. EXHAUSTION_WATCH — Extension or loss of momentum detected.
8. INVALIDATED — Underlying setup no longer valid.
9. EXPIRED — Setup exceeded its eligibility window.

Transitions must use completed-candle information and explicit rules.

Do not force every setup to pass through every state.

Some early momentum setups may become confirmed without a pullback.

Use the state machine to prevent repeated alerts and explain the current setup status.

